error[E0277]: a transition body must return its outputs, or a `Result` of them
  --> tests/ui/fail_slot_type.rs:16:62
   |
16 |     b.transition("Wrong slot", (TakeEdge(inbox),), (notes,), |n: u32| (n,));
   |       ---------- required by a bound introduced by this call ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `(u32,)` is not a transition outcome
   |
   = help: the trait `IntoOutcome<(PlaceRef<Note>,), _>` is not implemented for `(u32,)`
   = note: positional: outputs `(PlaceRef<Note>,)` want a tuple of that many slots, where slot i is `T`, `Option<T>` or `Vec<T>` for the type of output place i, and `()` for no outputs at all
   = note: routed: a value that is not a tuple, whose every payload goes to the output place that holds its type — derive `Routed` on the enum or struct you return
   = note: either form may be wrapped in `Result<_, E>` where `E: std::error::Error + Send + Sync + 'static`; a `Result` always means failure, never routing
